items.evidence:
components/navigation/AppShell.jsx — the live CountBadge no longer takes a `tone` string into `var(--${tone})`. It resolves through a map and paints `background: shown ? t.bg : t.mark, color: t.fg`. The map is:
  danger:  { bg: "var(--danger-bg)",     fg: "var(--danger-text)",  mark: "var(--danger)" }
  warning: { bg: "var(--warning-bg)",    fg: "var(--warning-text)", mark: "var(--warning)" }
  success: { bg: "var(--success-bg)",    fg: "var(--success-text)", mark: "var(--success)" }
  info:    { bg: "var(--info-bg)",       fg: "var(--info-text)",    mark: "var(--info)" }
  neutral: { bg: "var(--neutral-bg)",    fg: "var(--neutral-text)", mark: "var(--neutral)" }
  accent:  { bg: "var(--accent-subtle)", fg: "var(--accent)",       mark: "var(--accent)" }
`color: "var(--text-inverse)"` is gone entirely.

HEXES FROM tokens/colors.css: --danger-bg:#FDECEC / --danger-text:#B32226; --warning-bg:#FDF4E6 / --warning-text:#7A4F0B; --success-bg:#E9F7EF / --success-text:#0D6B3E; --info-bg:#EAF2FE / --info-text:#175AC4; --neutral-bg:#F0F1F3 / --neutral-text:#585B60; --accent-subtle:#EEECFF / --accent:#5A4BFF.

WCAG RATIOS I COMPUTED MYSELF (sRGB relative luminance, (L1+0.05)/(L2+0.05)), EVERY TONE THE COMPONENT SUPPORTS:
  danger   #B32226 on #FDECEC = 5.79:1  PASS
  warning  #7A4F0B on #FDF4E6 = 6.53:1  PASS
  success  #0D6B3E on #E9F7EF = 5.96:1  PASS
  info     #175AC4 on #EAF2FE = 5.65:1  PASS
  neutral  #585B60 on #F0F1F3 = 6.03:1  PASS
  accent   #5A4BFF on #EEECFF = 4.65:1  PASS (tightest)
All six clear the 4.5:1 floor. The old pairing I re-measured for confirmation: #FFFFFF on --danger #E5484D = 3.91:1 FAIL — exactly the 3.91 figure the register cites, and it no longer occurs anywhere in the component.

This matches components/data/Chip.jsx's Badge, the pattern 1b names as correct — its map is `danger: ["var(--danger-text)", "var(--danger-bg)"]` etc., with the same `accent: ["var(--accent)", "var(--accent-subtle)"]` exception and the same reason in comment: "[0] sets the WORDS, so it is the -text partner. --accent is the one that stays plain: it measures 4.65:1 on --accent-subtle and clears the floor unaided." tokens/colors.css's law — "Semantic colours are MARKS (dots, bars, fills, tints). Their -text partners are the only ones allowed to set words" — is obeyed. Teaching surfaces carry the same measured numbers: AppShell.d.ts — "danger 5.79, warning 6.53, success 5.96, info 5.65, neutral 6.03, accent 4.65"; AppShell.prompt.md — "white on `--danger`: **3.91:1**, under the 4.5 floor... `--danger-text` on `--danger-bg` measures **5.79:1**; no tone in the map is under 4.65"; AppRail.prompt.md, appnav.card.html and app-shell.card.html all state "5.79:1".

